# Judge item J0729

Does the finding describe the labelled defect? `describes`, `partially`, or `does-not-describe`.

## Finding

``` text
head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py:2544 — The chain walk's `except ChevalError` arm hard-aborts on the new `AgyOptInRequiredError` (a `ConfigError`). Every stock Google chain in the catalog terminates at `google:gemini-headless` (model-config.yaml:216, 228, 248, 262, 289, 309), so with the shipped default (opt-in off) any Google HTTP hop failure that walks to the terminal now exits INVALID_CONFIG "agy headless route is opt-in", masking the real upstream failure (RETRIES_EXHAUSTED / RATE_LIMIT) and contradicting the PR's own contract that a gated hop is "not planned, never a failed voice". The walker (or chain_resolver) must drop or skip an opt-in-gated hop instead of surfacing its refusal as the invocation's error.
head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py:2552 — `failure_class: opt_in_required` never reaches the wire: `_error_json(_e.code, str(_e), retryable=…)` discards `_e.context`, and the models_failed row at line 2549 records `error_class: "UNKNOWN"`. The "machine-readable seam planners read" promised in types.py:506, agy_headless_adapter.py:40 and docs/migration/v2.0-model-generation-floor.md:284 does not exist in stderr JSON or the MODELINV envelope; either plumb `context.failure_class` into both or drop the claim.
head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/loader.py:122 — `agy_opt_in_enabled` re-reads and deep-merges the whole system catalog (`.claude/defaults/model-config.yaml`, ~1500 lines) plus the project config on every call, and it is called from `complete()`, `health_check()` …
```

